      "author": "claude",
      "summary": "Block H's first hardware run: 4 of 6 doses exited scale-error and neither completed target is a measurement, so the run records the controller fault rather than salt's dose accuracy.",
      "detail": "The block H sequencing, thresholds, per-target summary and the new DOSE block letter all behaved exactly as designed, so the run validates the code path. The doses themselves did not: the three-phase doser still reads the balance through scale.read_stable(), which requires the A&D to assert ST, and the balance holds ST for only 0-2 percent of frames once the rig is actuating. Dose 1 is the same fault at the tare step -- the tare was silently refused while unstable, so the doser saw the 7.54 g already in the beaker from the feed diagnostic and declared overshoot without turning the auger. Dose 2 is the only dose that ran its controller to completion, and it overshot a 50 mg target by 7.5 mg on a single fine increment. qc.verdict set from the run-time placeholder 'ok' to doser-scale-unreadable; valid_for_cross_powder_comparison stays false.",
